    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the order, headlined by **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.41). Both benefit immensely from a favorable matchup against Anthony Kay, whose 4.74 xERA signals a high-leverage opportunity for our core. **Christian Yelich** (74.33) also projects as an elite play; his matchup against Ryan Feltner in a hitter-friendly environment, combined with a significant platoon advantage and a slow opposing delivery that screams stolen base potential, makes him a priority start today. **Kazuma Okamoto** (64.24) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) round out our high-efficiency anchors, both buoyed by prime lineup positioning and strong park factors.\n\nStrategic decisions for today were heavily influenced by the scarcity of stolen bases, which forced a difficult choice regarding our bench. **Caleb Durbin** (48.74) was the closest candidate to cracking the lineup, narrowly missing out due to a difficult matchup against Ryan Weathers. While **Caleb Durbin** offers elite speed, the optimizer favored the higher overall run-production profile of **Junior Caminero** (54.47), despite the latter\u2019s tough matchup against Ryan Gusto. We are monitoring **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.67) closely; while his speed is a massive asset, his score takes a hit from a significant platoon disadvantage against Robbie Ray and a tough opposing catcher. All managers should note that these scores assume projected batting orders; any last-minute defensive adjustments for **Gary Sanchez** or **Luke Raley** could impact their volatility in a narrow scoring environment.",
